---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { t } from '../../i18n';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('about.title')}
  description={`About the author behind this ${SITE.title} site.`}
>
 <section class="page-head section">
  <p class="eyebrow">{t('about.eyebrow')}</p>
  <h1>Building clear systems and useful tools.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I’m Rodrigo Mecheri, a software engineer who likes building things, figuring out how they work,
    and learning something new along the way.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section prose-grid">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
    <h2>I like understanding how things work.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <p>
      I work mostly on backend software, but I’ve always been interested in what happens beyond the
      code itself — how systems store and move data, deal with failures, communicate with each other,
      and behave when things don't go as planned.
    </p>
    <p>
      I learn best by building. Some projects start because I want to understand a particular
      technology, others because I have an idea I want to try. I don't mind going down a rabbit hole
      if I find something interesting along the way.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">This site</p>
    <h2>A place for things I’m working on.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <p>
      I use this site to share projects, notes, experiments, and things I've learned. Some of them
      will be finished, some won't. That's part of the point.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
